github.com/Code-Hex/vz/v3 v3.7.1, patched in socket.go: newVirtioSocketConnection dups the vsock fd and closes only the dup, because the VZVirtioSocketConnection owns the fd and closes it itself (SHARD-462).
Also in socket.go: a new ConnectHandler method exposes the framework's completion callback without the blocking channel receive that upstream Connect uses, so a connect to a port nobody listens on leaves no goroutine behind; both connect paths key the completion on a monotonic registry id instead of a cgo.Handle, so cancel reclaims the slot a never-answered dial would otherwise leak and a late callback finds the slot gone instead of resolving a freed handle (SHARD-619).
